  "summary": "The paper studies a gate-based QSVM fraud detector on the Kaggle credit-card dataset (284,807 transactions, 492 fraud cases, 0.172% fraud rate) using 4, 8, and 10 qubits/features. The best reported result is 98.8% accuracy, 0.962 F1, 0.945 recall, and 0.992 AUC with Quantum-SMOTE, compared with 92.4% accuracy, 0.907 F1, 0.881 recall, and 0.972 AUC for undersampling; classical SVM reaches 95.1% accuracy at 10 features versus 98.8% for QSVM.",
